File Index

/RightSidebar.tsx
Purpose: Fixed right-side panel (StatusBlock: tick + vitals + enemy + ancillary, plus room/compass). Custom-HUD-layout branch extracted StatusBlock's enemy-tracking state (enemyUi/damageChunk, the event:fighting:opponent listener and its staleness ticker) into the shared useOpponentStatus hook so both this classic sidebar and the compact layout's CompactVitalsRow consume the same logic instead of duplicating it.

/AccountModal.tsx
Purpose: Phase D — optional cloud-account panel (mirrors ConnectModal/LibraryModal's {isOpen,onClose,connectionId} shape). Logged-out: a single "Log in" button (gameSso.startLogin, which opens a POPUP — never navigates this window, so the game connection survives; the button shows a waiting state and the panel updates itself when the popup lands). Logged-in: save/load this connection's scripts+plugins to/from the cloud (via useAccountModal.ts) and log out. Never gates any existing functionality — logged out remains the default, fully-supported state. Phase E updated the blurb copy to mention library writings (parchment/notes/books) alongside scripts/plugins, and to say Load only replaces scripts/plugins — library content is merged, never deleted.

/AutoLevelingModal.tsx
Purpose: The original ~2500-line auto-leveling modal, superseded by AutoLevelingWizard.tsx. As of 2026-09-13 it is genuinely dead code — MainContainer.tsx's `localStorage['autoleveling.wizard']` opt-out ternary that could still render this was removed outright (see AutoLevelingWizard.tsx's entry below) — but it has NOT been deleted yet, left in place pending user confirmation before a bigger deletion pass (.module.scss alongside it, same status).

/AutoLevelingWizard.tsx
Purpose: THE ONLY auto-leveling UI as of 2026-09-13 — the `localStorage['autoleveling.wizard']` opt-out escape hatch to AutoLevelingModal was removed from MainContainer.tsx (live-playtest feedback: Weight wasn't "gated behind a flag", it's just part of this wizard) rather than left for step 13; AutoLevelingModal.tsx/.module.scss are now unreferenced dead code, not yet deleted. A linear 7-step wizard (Area / Targets / Combat / Rest / Weight / Review / Start — Rest inserted 2026-09-12, Weight inserted 2026-09-13) sharing the same `useAutoLeveling` props via a MainContainer shared-props IIFE. Step panels live in `components/wizard/` (AreaStep, TargetsStep, CombatStep, RestStep, WeightStep, ReviewStep + useWizardDraft/useCharacterLevel/dsl-classes/FilterableSelect). 2026-09-13: a step-header "Apply live changes" bar (visible while running, only on Combat/Rest/Weight — each with its own precise hint text since Combat/Rest each mix a hot-swappable part with a frozen one) calls `setConfig(draftToConfig(draft))` on demand for the 3 config paths the engine already re-fetches fresh per-call (fight-commands, rest during-round, weight); a separate "Pause to edit" hint on Targets covers everything else (targets/buffs/route/rest-start-end-of-round), which only ever picks up an edit via the engine's pause→resume resync (`refreshRunSnapshot()`), never live. Area route + targets come from the C#-served IndexedDB cache (`features/autoleveling/autoleveling-content.ts`, with a ⟳ refresh control that bypasses both the client IndexedDB cache and web-server's own in-memory cache via `?refresh=1`); buff/fight overlays + custom targets + class pref from `autoleveling-user-data.ts`, seeded into the draft on area selection. Start step is a run-monitor wired to the real engine controls, plus (2026-09-12) a "Last kill" row from `useAutoLeveling`'s separate `xpProgress` state (survives status transitions, cleared on a fresh Start, hidden unless actively running). The draft→AutoLevelConfig build + retiring the old modal is a later plan step (.ai-plans/20260909-0739-autoleveling-redesign.md). Draggable, matches AutoLevelingModal's shell.

/LibraryModal.tsx
Purpose: The parchment/notes/books editor (tabs, list+editor split, Scribe panel that pushes drafts into the live game session as commands, JSON export/import, DSL color preview). Phase E added tag-based grouping to all three sidebar lists (parchmentByTag/booksByTag memos, notesBySpool now nests a tag sub-group within each spool — reuses mobile's groupByTag algorithm), a tag input in the editor header, cursor-tracked line/char-limit stats under the body textarea (getLineStats/getWarnings from library-types.ts), and tag/recipients round-tripping through the export/import bundle and handleSave's three branches — closing the editor-parity gap with the mobile client's book-editor. Organizations Phase 2 Step 5 added an 'organizations' tab as its own top-level pane (`{tab === 'organizations' && <OrganizationsPane />}`, not threaded into the parchment/notes/books showList branches) — see OrganizationsPane.tsx. UNSAVED-CHANGES GUARD: every exit that would drop the draft (item select incl. the Scribe pickers, tab switch, New, JSON import, close, and the browser tab via useBeforeUnloadGuard) goes through confirmLoseChanges, which judges the open tab's draft against what is saved (features/library/unsavedChanges.ts) and, for the Organizations tab, relies on OrganizationsPane's onDirtyChange report. Clicking the item already open never asks. Colors and Scratch are not guarded (nothing saved to lose). Tests: LibraryModal.unsaved.test.tsx.

/OrganizationsPane.tsx
Purpose: Organizations Phase 2 Step 5 — game-client's Organizations tab (Library modal), extracted out of LibraryModal.tsx rather than growing its already-dense tab={'x'} branches further. Org + acting-as-character pickers, role-gated (client-side, server enforces regardless) content CRUD across parchment/notes/books, an N-level recursive category-folder tree (CategoryTreeNode, built from org-content-types.ts — groupByTag doesn't generalize to real nesting). No org creation/invites/roles/bans/revisions/audit here — those stay web-dashboard-only. Fetches live on every org/content-type switch, no IndexedDB mirror (multi-writer shared data with a rotating per-org key makes a local cache a staleness-bug generator, reasoned through in the Phase 2 plan doc's step 5 log). Imports LibraryModal.module.scss directly (existing precedent: CompassBlockMobile/MiscPane/PluginsPage do the same for a sibling component's module).

/UserScriptSandboxModal.tsx
Purpose: Triggers/Aliases/Timers/Globals/Variables editor. Gotcha: the modal stays mounted when closed and its close handler resets globalLanguage to JavaScript and globalDraft to empty; the Globals draft-sync effect therefore lists isOpen as a dependency, or a saved JavaScript global reopens blank with Unsaved changes shown (and Save would overwrite it with nothing). Regression test: UserScriptSandboxModal.globals.test.tsx.

/ScriptingHelpModal.tsx
Purpose: The in-app Scripting Help (Help > Scripting…): a section nav plus one scrollable page of player-facing guidance. Its Global Scripts section describes the invoke contract (globals by name in JS/TS, one shared Lua/Python program, runGlobal results and callbacks) and must stay in step with docs/scripting/scripting-summary.md, docs/features/scripting-and-sharing.md and the Scripting page on the C# site (DSL repo, Views/Library/Scripting.cshtml). Adding a section means adding its id to SectionId AND NAV_SECTIONS. CSS modules resolve to undefined under jest, so tests cannot assert the active-nav class. Tests: ScriptingHelpModal.test.tsx.
 UNSAVED-CHANGES GUARD: select item, + New, content-type buttons and the organization picker all go through confirmLoseChanges; the pane reports dirty + title to LibraryModal via onDirtyChange (and false on unmount) so the Library can guard tab-switch/close, and holds the browser tab itself. An item just saved is not 'dirty' while the reloaded list has not arrived yet (awaitingReload). Tests: OrganizationsPane.unsaved.test.tsx.